  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through Saturday)\nIssued at 201 AM MDT Sun Aug 9 2026\n\nMore noticeable changes are expected to begin by Tuesday as a much \nlarger pattern shift currently unfolding across the Pacific Ocean \nimpacts the monsoon circulation across the southwest CONUS. The \naforementioned speed max will continue progressing northwest from AZ \ninto the Great Basin Tuesday while a subtle H5 trough deepens along \nthe U.S. West Coast thru Wednesday. The monsoon plume will begin to \nstand up over AZ and western NM as 700-500mb layer flow becomes more \nsoutherly and the H5 high center migrates east toward TX. The latest \n00Z ECMWF has trended more bullish again with a robust monsoon burst \npattern over the region Tuesday thru Saturday. Each day will be a \ndifferent flavor but the risk for storms with locally heavy rainfall \nand potential flash flooding will increase over the region. Temps \nwill also trend closer to normal which will feel pleasant compared\nto the brutal heatwave that has plagued the area since late July.",
